---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import HeroEmber from "../components/HeroEmber.astro";
---

<Base
  current="manifesto"
  title="Manifesto — Slow Lit Labs"
  description="The lab is the proof. Slow Lit is operated by the agents we build."
>
  <section class="shell section-hero pb-12 md:pb-20">
    <div class="measure-wide">
      <p class="mono rise rise-1">§ Manifesto</p>

      <h1 class="display-hero mt-12 md:mt-16 rise rise-2">
        The lab<br />is the proof.<HeroEmber />
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell section-tight reveal">
    <div class="measure prose-body has-dropcap" style="font-size: 1.1875rem;">
      <p>
        Most AI companies sell a future they don&apos;t live in. They publish
        papers about agents while their own work is done by humans. They demo
        systems that don&apos;t survive contact with reality.
      </p>
      <p>We took a different bet.</p>
      <p>
        Slow Lit is being built to be operated by the agents we make. As Ember
        matures, more of our work moves to the agents we ship: research operations, support, writing, code review, hiring. When our models
        get better, our company gets better. When they fail, we feel it
        before any customer does.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is not a marketing position. It is the only honest way to build
        agents that work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell section reveal">
    <hr class="rule mb-12 md:mb-20" />
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 md:gap-20">
      <div class="md:col-span-3 sticky-label">
        <p class="mono">§ What we believe</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-8 measure-wide">
        <ol class="numbered">
          <li class="numbered-item">
            <span class="num">01</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="display-medium">Build it. Use it. Then sell it.</h3>
              <p class="prose-body mt-6">
                The order matters. A product that hasn&apos;t survived its
                makers won&apos;t survive its users.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="numbered-item">
            <span class="num">02</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="display-medium">Small teams ship better models.</h3>
              <p class="prose-body mt-6">
                Talent density beats headcount. We hire people who have
                shipped, not people who have studied shipping.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="numbered-item">
            <span class="num">03</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="display-medium">Europe can build frontier AI.</h3>
              <p class="prose-body mt-6">
                The talent is here. The seriousness is here. What was missing
                was the willingness to act like it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="numbered-item">
            <span class="num">04</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="display-medium">Agents are colleagues, not features.</h3>
              <p class="prose-body mt-6">
                An agent that runs for an hour and dies is a script. An agent
                that runs for a year and remembers is a coworker. We build
                the second kind.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell section reveal">
    <hr class="rule mb-12 md:mb-20" />
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 md:gap-20">
      <div class="md:col-span-3 sticky-label">
        <p class="mono">§ What we are not</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-8 measure-wide">
        <h2 class="display-large">
          Not a chatbot company. Not an enterprise wrapper.
        </h2>
        <div class="prose-body mt-12">
          <p>
            We are not building a foundation model to license to OpenAI
            customers.
          </p>
          <p>
            We are a lab. We do research. We ship products. The two feed
            each other.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-16">
          <a href="/ember" class="link-arrow">
            About Ember <span class="arrow">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
